# The games APPS lists. scripts/gen_games.py exports each at its pin (git archive, from a local clone
# found in GAMES_REPOS, default this repo's parent) and writes build/games/{games.mk,games.cmake,games.h}.
# A game by anyone outside our seats needs Michael's word before it is listed (decision 59); every
# entry passes soroban's gate. Format and manifest: the header of scripts/gen_games.py.
# ID   REPO          PIN                                       LICENCE                    MANIFEST
# Babal: arcade's port of Babal by Christian Mauduit, gitlab.com/liberecofr/babal (public domain, the Unlicense)
babal  stu32-arcade  5947c16d6b96928b5511129a6024c2ea570d152e  MIT                        games/babal/stu32-game.txt
# AIM: arcade's, four tiles to the round's target in RPN (Michael's decision 71; stu32-arcade docs/aim.md)
aim    stu32-arcade  5fe8ceaceedd3d4aac5513f1c7e713b45aa24509  MIT                        games/aim/stu32-game.txt
# LAND: arcade's, set the ship down on a pad (Michael's decision 71; stu32-arcade docs/land.md)
land   stu32-arcade  e20cd98bed21758b256604011ae11b67a809d671  MIT                        games/land/stu32-game.txt
# SNAKE: arcade's, eat, grow, and keep off the walls and yourself (Michael's decision 71; stu32-arcade docs/snake.md)
snake  stu32-arcade  a01609b50a074660ff29ba72d7a50a4cca2fc6c5  MIT                        games/snake/stu32-game.txt
# MINES: arcade's, clear the field with no guess ever needed (Michael's decision 71; stu32-arcade docs/mines.md)
mines  stu32-arcade  7344045c918f2818963ab5946aca3f3d3fad644f  MIT                        games/mines/stu32-game.txt
